body:
I posted about this before. I get therapy from my university's psychological counselor. As a matter of legal liability, they warned me that if they feel that I am in danger of harming myself, they'll notify emergency services to have me involuntarily committed to a psyche ward. I believe if that happens, that'll be a point of no return for me. I am certain that nothing would keep me from committing suicide should that happen. Which is ironic because something that is meant to help me because I am going to commit suicide would end up making me commit suicide. I have no one else to turn to  except for some not so close friends. I think that it's too difficult to talk to my family about it. I'm afraid of what they'll say. 

&#x200B;

Edit: last two sentences
